1
00:00:00,959 --> 00:00:03,920
♪ Oh, Mr. Tailor ♪

2
00:00:04,004 --> 00:00:08,341
[MAMANG SASTRE PLAYING]

3
00:00:09,342 --> 00:00:10,844
♪ Oh, Mr. Tailor ♪

4
00:00:10,927 --> 00:00:12,971
♪ Holding the scissors ♪

5
00:00:16,725 --> 00:00:17,726
[Oscar] Who-- who are you?

6
00:00:17,809 --> 00:00:19,477
What are you doing here?

7
00:00:19,561 --> 00:00:20,228
[Atoy]  Oka?

8
00:00:20,311 --> 00:00:22,147
[Janine]  Who’s that with him, Mommy?

9
00:00:22,230 --> 00:00:25,442
I wonder where Tatoy’s best friend is.

10
00:00:25,525 --> 00:00:26,860
[Oscar] We need to leave now.

11
00:00:26,943 --> 00:00:28,153
[explosion & rumbling]

12
00:00:28,236 --> 00:00:29,404
[Cita]  I wonder where Atoy went.

13
00:00:29,487 --> 00:00:31,573
[Jesabel]  What were they even
doing out at sea?

14
00:00:31,656 --> 00:00:32,741
[Atoy]  Help! Over here!

15
00:00:32,824 --> 00:00:33,783
[Nurse] What happened to him?

16
00:00:33,867 --> 00:00:35,160
He got into an accident

17
00:00:35,243 --> 00:00:36,661
on the ship we were on.

18
00:00:36,745 --> 00:00:38,580
What were you doing on that ship?

19
00:00:38,663 --> 00:00:40,540
What do you know about Grey Shadow?

20
00:00:41,291 --> 00:00:42,083
Why were you there?

21
00:00:42,167 --> 00:00:43,752
[Atoy]  It’s been more than ten years

22
00:00:43,835 --> 00:00:44,836
since we were last together,

23
00:00:44,919 --> 00:00:46,087
and then suddenly you show up.

24
00:00:46,171 --> 00:00:48,590
Buddy, I never wanted to be there.

25
00:00:48,673 --> 00:00:49,674
[explosions & rumbling]

26
00:00:49,758 --> 00:00:53,261
[Oscar] Do you still remember
the last operation we worked on together?

27
00:00:53,344 --> 00:00:54,345
[explosions & rumbling]

28
00:00:54,429 --> 00:00:57,140
Sister Carmel, I’m Captain Oscar Asuncion.

29
00:00:57,223 --> 00:00:59,559
[Oscar] We’re here to rescue you.

30
00:01:00,393 --> 00:01:01,770
[music swells]

31
00:01:02,353 --> 00:01:03,104
[bomb blips]

32
00:01:03,188 --> 00:01:04,439
[explosions & rumbling]

33
00:01:04,522 --> 00:01:06,441
[Oscar on the radio] I’m surrounded
by hostiles.

34
00:01:06,524 --> 00:01:07,776
Bomb my location.

35
00:01:07,859 --> 00:01:09,736
What? No.

36
00:01:09,819 --> 00:01:10,862
I’m coming to get you.

37
00:01:11,488 --> 00:01:12,947
Don’t come back for me.

38
00:01:13,531 --> 00:01:15,700
Striker One, this is Captain Padua.

39
00:01:15,784 --> 00:01:16,618
[Atoy]  Initiate air strike.

40
00:01:16,701 --> 00:01:18,912
[Oscar] I never gave that order, ’Toy.

41
00:01:18,995 --> 00:01:20,205
They had already captured me.

42
00:01:20,288 --> 00:01:21,331
There was nothing I could do.

43
00:01:21,414 --> 00:01:22,332
Buddy, who are they?

44
00:01:22,415 --> 00:01:23,958
They’re Obsidian operatives.

45
00:01:24,042 --> 00:01:25,543
What did they do to you, buddy?

46
00:01:25,627 --> 00:01:28,254
[Oscar] Nonstop, over and over.

47
00:01:28,338 --> 00:01:28,880
They hurt me.

48
00:01:28,963 --> 00:01:30,548
They broke me.

49
00:01:30,632 --> 00:01:32,217
More than ten years of my life

50
00:01:32,300 --> 00:01:33,426
were destroyed.

51
00:01:33,510 --> 00:01:34,928
That was one of the…

52
00:01:35,011 --> 00:01:37,847
hardest decisions I ever made, Oka.

53
00:01:37,931 --> 00:01:39,474
I understand you, bro.

54
00:01:39,557 --> 00:01:42,060
So, I hope you don’t think…

55
00:01:42,143 --> 00:01:43,102
that after all this time,

56
00:01:43,186 --> 00:01:43,978
I’m still blaming you.

57
00:01:44,062 --> 00:01:46,189
[Oscar] Looks like my prayers to…

58
00:01:46,272 --> 00:01:47,982
Saint Anthony really worked.

59
00:01:48,733 --> 00:01:50,610
You still managed to find me, brother.

60
00:01:50,693 --> 00:01:52,570
[Oscar] Right?

61
00:01:53,488 --> 00:01:55,323
Is Daddy Tatoy still not here?

62
00:01:55,406 --> 00:01:58,159
[Woman on the TV] And seven, eight,

63
00:01:59,410 --> 00:02:00,662
Where is he?

64
00:02:00,745 --> 00:02:02,789
[On screen] We have a developing report.

65
00:02:02,872 --> 00:02:06,209
A soldier who was presumed dead

66
00:02:06,292 --> 00:02:07,544
more than ten years ago

67
00:02:07,627 --> 00:02:08,920
has been found.

68
00:02:09,003 --> 00:02:13,716
He is Oscar Asuncion, who was believed to
have died in an encounter

69
00:02:13,800 --> 00:02:16,511
against the Red Front rebel group.

70
00:02:16,594 --> 00:02:18,930
Oscar Asuncion is recognized

71
00:02:19,013 --> 00:02:20,932
- Wait.
- as the Hero of the

72
00:02:21,015 --> 00:02:22,725
- Isn’t that…
- “Carmel-Drilon…”

73
00:02:22,809 --> 00:02:24,435
Rescue Operation. According to our source,

74
00:02:24,519 --> 00:02:26,062
… Tatoy’s best friend?

75
00:02:26,146 --> 00:02:28,022
… in the photo album?

76
00:02:28,106 --> 00:02:30,275
… following an unusual explosion

77
00:02:30,358 --> 00:02:32,068
at the Vizaray Coast.

78
00:02:32,152 --> 00:02:33,736
Rocky Magno reporting.

79
00:02:33,820 --> 00:02:34,571
[phone blips]

80
00:02:34,654 --> 00:02:37,157
[suspicious music playing]

81
00:02:45,123 --> 00:02:46,124
Your daddy is on the way.

82
00:02:46,207 --> 00:02:48,793
[theme music playing]

83
00:02:48,877 --> 00:02:50,253
♪ Oh, Mr. Tailor… ♪

84
00:02:50,336 --> 00:02:53,840
["Mamang Sastre" playing]

85
00:02:57,302 --> 00:02:59,387
♪ Wait a moment, Mister Tailor ♪

86
00:02:59,470 --> 00:03:00,096
♪ Can you be the one ♪

87
00:03:00,179 --> 00:03:02,098
♪ To sew the hole in my polo ♪

88
00:03:02,181 --> 00:03:04,934
♪ That’s right under the armpit ♪

89
00:03:05,018 --> 00:03:07,103
♪ In every cut of cloth ♪

90
00:03:07,186 --> 00:03:08,688
♪ There’s a secret behind it ♪

91
00:03:08,771 --> 00:03:10,607
♪ If your measurements are wrong ♪

92
00:03:10,690 --> 00:03:15,153
the whole fit turns crooked… ♪

93
00:03:15,236 --> 00:03:15,862
[gunshots]

94
00:03:15,945 --> 00:03:17,614
♪ Oh, Mr. Tailor ♪

95
00:03:17,697 --> 00:03:19,782
♪ Holding the scissors ♪

96
00:03:19,866 --> 00:03:21,576
[music swells]

97
00:03:21,659 --> 00:03:23,328
(Fix this)

98
00:03:23,411 --> 00:03:24,746
[music fades]

99
00:03:25,538 --> 00:03:26,706
- Still not here?
- Geez--

100
00:03:28,124 --> 00:03:28,708
[clicks tongue]

101
00:03:28,791 --> 00:03:31,753
I can’t get in touch with Atoy.

102
00:03:31,836 --> 00:03:32,420
Where could he be?

103
00:03:32,503 --> 00:03:34,130
Could he have been left at sea?

104
00:03:34,213 --> 00:03:36,090
That’s impossible. Not him.

105
00:03:36,174 --> 00:03:37,383
Why can’t I reach him?

106
00:03:37,467 --> 00:03:39,302
Maybe there’s just no signal.

107
00:03:39,969 --> 00:03:41,054
[Paldo]  Emerson!

108
00:03:42,388 --> 00:03:43,848
Who’s that with you? Why…

109
00:03:45,350 --> 00:03:46,851
Why aren’t you introducing me?

110
00:03:46,935 --> 00:03:48,228
Oh, this is…

111
00:03:48,311 --> 00:03:49,896
Uh, Je-- ah--

112
00:03:49,979 --> 00:03:50,563
Ah, ah--

113
00:03:50,647 --> 00:03:53,191
I’m Paldo.

114
00:03:54,108 --> 00:03:56,361
I’m the captain here in Tabang Lupa.

115
00:03:56,444 --> 00:03:58,363
Oh, Captain Paldo.

116
00:03:58,446 --> 00:04:01,157
Oh, and I’m Jesabel.

117
00:04:01,241 --> 00:04:02,617
Hmm, do you…

118
00:04:02,700 --> 00:04:03,451
Do you have a boyfriend?

119
00:04:03,534 --> 00:04:04,410
Oh, no. I’m single.

120
00:04:04,494 --> 00:04:05,036
Ah, really?

121
00:04:05,119 --> 00:04:05,662
Mmm-hmm.

122
00:04:05,745 --> 00:04:07,664
Jesabel, as in Jesabel…

123
00:04:07,747 --> 00:04:08,831
Not a fish, okay?

124
00:04:08,915 --> 00:04:10,583
Because I’m not fishy.

125
00:04:10,667 --> 00:04:14,504
Yes. I’m Jesabel. J-E-S-E--

126
00:04:14,587 --> 00:04:18,424
Je-- Uh, J-E-S-A-B-L--

127
00:04:19,634 --> 00:04:21,594
Never mind, just Jesabel. Mmm-hmm.

128
00:04:22,887 --> 00:04:23,930
You’re so pretty.

129
00:04:24,013 --> 00:04:24,764
Knock on wood.

130
00:04:24,847 --> 00:04:26,307
[Denden chuckles sarcastically]
I’ll come visit you sometime.

131
00:04:26,391 --> 00:04:28,101
[Denden]   And I’m Geraldine.

132
00:04:28,184 --> 00:04:33,523
G-E-R-A-L-D-I-N-E! Denden!

133
00:04:34,232 --> 00:04:36,985
[Others]  Den-den-den-den!

134
00:04:37,568 --> 00:04:39,988
Oh no! Here we go!

135
00:04:40,071 --> 00:04:41,406
[clears throat]

136
00:04:41,489 --> 00:04:44,617
And, My Loves, why are you together, huh?

137
00:04:44,701 --> 00:04:46,911
[Others]  Den-den-den-den!

138
00:04:46,995 --> 00:04:48,079
[stutters]

139
00:04:48,663 --> 00:04:53,459
Uh, ma-- uh, My Loves, let me explain.

140
00:04:53,543 --> 00:04:55,003
We’re not together.

141
00:04:55,086 --> 00:04:56,963
We're just, uh…

142
00:04:57,046 --> 00:04:57,922
We just happened to meet here.

143
00:04:58,006 --> 00:04:59,841
We're not on a date.

144
00:04:59,924 --> 00:05:01,342
Right, right.

145
00:05:02,343 --> 00:05:02,927
Yeah, we just happened to meet here.

146
00:05:03,011 --> 00:05:05,596
So, it just so happened that you
went home together too?

147
00:05:05,680 --> 00:05:07,348
[Others]  Den-den- den-den!

148
00:05:07,932 --> 00:05:09,600
No, no, no!

149
00:05:09,684 --> 00:05:12,103
No, My Loves, it's just…

150
00:05:12,186 --> 00:05:14,439
The… the… the…

151
00:05:14,522 --> 00:05:15,064
The…

152
00:05:15,148 --> 00:05:16,399
[titters]

153
00:05:16,482 --> 00:05:17,400
The way…

154
00:05:20,611 --> 00:05:22,030
We're both headed there, right?

155
00:05:22,113 --> 00:05:23,906
There's no other-- there’s no other way…

156
00:05:23,990 --> 00:05:26,409
So, uh…

157
00:05:27,035 --> 00:05:29,037
Maybe don't get mad at me right now,

158
00:05:29,120 --> 00:05:31,164
because there's a bigger problem.

159
00:05:31,247 --> 00:05:33,374
It’s Atoy… Atoy…

160
00:05:34,042 --> 00:05:35,835
Atoy is missing right now.

161
00:05:35,918 --> 00:05:37,170
That doesn't seem likely.

162
00:05:37,253 --> 00:05:38,838
I saw Atoy earlier, Denden.

163
00:05:38,921 --> 00:05:40,590
- I think he passed by here.
- No. He didn't.

164
00:05:40,673 --> 00:05:43,301
- He did pass by here.
- What do you mean? Where?

165
00:05:43,384 --> 00:05:44,469
He passed by here earlier.

166
00:05:45,094 --> 00:05:46,054
You're just making excuses…

167
00:05:46,137 --> 00:05:47,889
So, he did pass by here.

168
00:05:47,972 --> 00:05:49,348
… so Denden won't get mad at you.

169
00:05:49,432 --> 00:05:51,309
No.

170
00:05:51,934 --> 00:05:52,602
Wait.

171
00:05:52,685 --> 00:05:54,353
You seem to be sweating.

172
00:05:54,437 --> 00:05:55,480
[Paldo]  Oh, geez.

173
00:05:56,689 --> 00:05:57,899
I'm not sweating.

174
00:05:58,983 --> 00:06:00,359
Actually…

175
00:06:00,443 --> 00:06:01,319
Hey, wipe yourself off!

176
00:06:01,402 --> 00:06:04,572
[lively chatter]

177
00:06:04,655 --> 00:06:07,283
De-- Denden--

178
00:06:08,618 --> 00:06:10,828
[Others]  Den-den-den-den…

179
00:06:14,040 --> 00:06:17,001
Handsome-guy problems, huh?

180
00:06:17,085 --> 00:06:18,544
- Daddy!
- Tatoy!

181
00:06:18,628 --> 00:06:20,505
Oh, whoa! How are you?

182
00:06:20,588 --> 00:06:22,965
- I missed you.
- Mmm…

183
00:06:25,093 --> 00:06:26,594
Oh, I brought something for you.

184
00:06:26,677 --> 00:06:27,553
[gasps]

185
00:06:27,637 --> 00:06:28,221
Lanzones.

186
00:06:28,304 --> 00:06:29,305
Delicious! Thank you!

187
00:06:29,388 --> 00:06:30,223
It’s delicious!

188
00:06:30,848 --> 00:06:32,517
That's my favorite!

189
00:06:32,600 --> 00:06:33,559
[Ibyang]  Let's eat.

190
00:06:35,019 --> 00:06:37,188
Love, you weren't answering my calls.

191
00:06:37,814 --> 00:06:39,440
Don't do that again, okay?

192
00:06:40,650 --> 00:06:41,442
Ah, sorry, Love.

193
00:06:41,526 --> 00:06:42,401
[sniffs]

194
00:06:42,485 --> 00:06:43,402
Uhm…

195
00:06:44,904 --> 00:06:47,031
My phone’s battery is drained.

196
00:06:47,115 --> 00:06:49,325
Then I delivered some suits to a client.

197
00:06:50,118 --> 00:06:50,993
I'm sorry.

198
00:06:52,453 --> 00:06:55,665
Uhm, Love, did you hear about the…

199
00:06:55,748 --> 00:06:57,458
man who was found at sea?

200
00:06:58,084 --> 00:06:59,877
The former soldier.

201
00:06:59,961 --> 00:07:00,711
It was on the news.

202
00:07:00,795 --> 00:07:01,671
We saw it earlier.

203
00:07:01,754 --> 00:07:02,755
Right, Ibyang?

204
00:07:02,839 --> 00:07:03,506
- Yes.
- Janine?

205
00:07:03,589 --> 00:07:05,883
We saw him on TV,

206
00:07:05,967 --> 00:07:08,719
The soldier who is Tatoy's friend.

207
00:07:08,803 --> 00:07:10,513
The one we saw in the picture.

208
00:07:10,596 --> 00:07:11,848
Uh-huh.

209
00:07:12,974 --> 00:07:15,935
Actually, I came from the hospital.

210
00:07:16,018 --> 00:07:16,853
Oh?

211
00:07:16,936 --> 00:07:17,812
I visited him.

212
00:07:17,895 --> 00:07:19,480
How is he?

213
00:07:20,314 --> 00:07:21,315
[Audrey]  Is he with his…

214
00:07:21,399 --> 00:07:22,817
family now?

215
00:07:23,526 --> 00:07:24,569
Not yet.

216
00:07:25,153 --> 00:07:28,448
In fact, he's actually here right now.

217
00:07:28,531 --> 00:07:29,740
Hmm?

218
00:07:29,824 --> 00:07:32,160
[ominous music playing]

219
00:07:32,243 --> 00:07:33,995
- Oscar.
- Good evening, everyone!

220
00:07:34,078 --> 00:07:36,664
[music continues]

221
00:07:38,541 --> 00:07:39,417
Good evening.

222
00:07:39,500 --> 00:07:40,585
[chuckles]

223
00:07:41,919 --> 00:07:42,753
[Atoy]  This is Audrey.

224
00:07:43,921 --> 00:07:45,631
And these are Ibyang and Janine.

225
00:07:45,715 --> 00:07:47,884
[music continues]

226
00:07:47,967 --> 00:07:49,051
Ah, Love…

227
00:07:50,553 --> 00:07:52,763
can Oka stay here for now?

228
00:07:55,141 --> 00:07:57,226
[music swells]

229
00:08:01,063 --> 00:08:03,441
Good evening, Oscar.

230
00:08:03,524 --> 00:08:04,692
[pensive music playing]

231
00:08:05,276 --> 00:08:09,030
Love, can I talk to you?

232
00:08:09,989 --> 00:08:11,240
Oh, sure.

233
00:08:11,324 --> 00:08:12,867
Buddy, just stay here for now, okay?

234
00:08:13,784 --> 00:08:16,204
[music continues]

235
00:08:17,872 --> 00:08:19,916
Would you like some langsat?

236
00:08:19,999 --> 00:08:21,667
Oh, no. I'm okay.

237
00:08:21,751 --> 00:08:23,836
Atoy and I already ate on the way here.

238
00:08:23,920 --> 00:08:25,671
But thanks for the offer.

239
00:08:26,380 --> 00:08:27,924
By the way, what are your names again?

240
00:08:28,007 --> 00:08:29,467
I'm Ibyang.

241
00:08:29,550 --> 00:08:30,218
[Oscar] Ibyang.

242
00:08:30,301 --> 00:08:31,302
And this is Janine.

243
00:08:31,385 --> 00:08:32,386
[Oscar] Janine!

244
00:08:32,762 --> 00:08:34,931
By the way, I'm…

245
00:08:35,014 --> 00:08:35,765
Uncle Oscar.

246
00:08:35,848 --> 00:08:37,975
Actually, just call me Uncle Oka.

247
00:08:38,643 --> 00:08:39,519
Oka.

248
00:08:39,602 --> 00:08:40,561
Oka, Oka.

249
00:08:40,645 --> 00:08:41,562
[chuckles]

250
00:08:41,646 --> 00:08:42,605
Okak, okak.

251
00:08:43,231 --> 00:08:44,315
Okak.

252
00:08:44,398 --> 00:08:45,441
[laughs]

253
00:08:46,234 --> 00:08:47,068
Oka.

254
00:08:47,151 --> 00:08:47,860
[chuckles]

255
00:08:50,196 --> 00:08:52,532
[ominous music playing]

256
00:08:52,615 --> 00:08:54,450
You definitely got it from someone.

257
00:08:55,785 --> 00:08:57,161
Your mommy is very beautiful.

258
00:08:59,914 --> 00:09:00,748
[music fades]

259
00:09:01,958 --> 00:09:02,792
[door closes]

260
00:09:03,918 --> 00:09:05,836
Are you sure about your decision?

261
00:09:07,171 --> 00:09:10,383
Aren't you rushing into it?

262
00:09:10,466 --> 00:09:12,426
I don't mean to sound rude, but…

263
00:09:14,428 --> 00:09:16,931
Love, I can't just leave Oka

264
00:09:17,014 --> 00:09:17,682
and abandon him.

265
00:09:17,765 --> 00:09:19,976
No family has come to claim him
at the hospital.

266
00:09:20,685 --> 00:09:21,811
He's my friend.

267
00:09:21,894 --> 00:09:23,771
I can't just leave him by himself.

268
00:09:23,854 --> 00:09:25,982
I understand that he's your friend.

269
00:09:26,649 --> 00:09:29,902
But ten years have passed.

270
00:09:30,653 --> 00:09:31,988
Do you really think he's still

271
00:09:32,071 --> 00:09:34,115
the same Oscar you once knew?

272
00:09:35,241 --> 00:09:36,826
What if you're letting

273
00:09:36,909 --> 00:09:38,953
a dangerous person into our home?

274
00:09:39,036 --> 00:09:39,870
No.

275
00:09:41,289 --> 00:09:42,748
Love, Oka is not a bad person.

276
00:09:44,458 --> 00:09:45,876
You don't know that.

277
00:09:46,419 --> 00:09:47,503
Why don't you just find

278
00:09:47,587 --> 00:09:48,963
somewhere else for him to stay?

279
00:09:49,046 --> 00:09:52,258
Like a hotel or an apartment
that he can rent.

280
00:09:52,925 --> 00:09:54,552
[Audrey]  Just not here, Love.

281
00:09:57,179 --> 00:09:58,264
Audrey, you know,

282
00:09:58,347 --> 00:09:59,765
I already left him behind once.

283
00:10:00,766 --> 00:10:02,935
And because I left him behind,

284
00:10:03,019 --> 00:10:04,645
he was captured by the enemy.

285
00:10:05,313 --> 00:10:06,856
Okay? And because of that,

286
00:10:06,939 --> 00:10:08,149
he lost his family.

287
00:10:08,232 --> 00:10:10,151
He lost everything.

288
00:10:11,193 --> 00:10:13,446
I just don't want him to feel
like he's all alone.

289
00:10:14,322 --> 00:10:14,947
Okay?

290
00:10:17,158 --> 00:10:20,328
Love, I hope you realize that…

291
00:10:20,411 --> 00:10:22,121
this is also my house,

292
00:10:22,788 --> 00:10:24,707
and our kids' house.

293
00:10:25,291 --> 00:10:29,462
And I'm not comfortable having someone
we don't know living here.

294
00:10:29,545 --> 00:10:34,383
[pensive music playing]

295
00:10:40,264 --> 00:10:41,349
Hmm?

296
00:10:49,190 --> 00:10:50,316
What were you doing here?

297
00:10:50,900 --> 00:10:53,444
[Janine]  Uhm, we were playing
hide-and-seek.

298
00:10:53,527 --> 00:10:56,530
Daddy took our picture when he found us.

299
00:10:56,614 --> 00:10:57,365
[Oscar] Hmm.

300
00:10:57,448 --> 00:10:59,659
Because someone squeezed
into my hiding spot.

301
00:10:59,742 --> 00:11:01,786
[Janine]  She could've hidden
somewhere else.

302
00:11:02,745 --> 00:11:04,580
[Ibyang]  Me?

303
00:11:04,664 --> 00:11:05,665
Yes.

304
00:11:06,248 --> 00:11:10,544
[Ibyang]  I got to that tree first!

305
00:11:10,628 --> 00:11:12,880
No, you were the one who squeezed in!

306
00:11:12,963 --> 00:11:13,798
I was there first!

307
00:11:13,881 --> 00:11:14,924
Hey, oops. Oops, oops, oops.

308
00:11:15,007 --> 00:11:16,842
Easy, easy, easy. Hold on.

309
00:11:17,426 --> 00:11:18,427
Oh, ouch. What?

310
00:11:18,511 --> 00:11:20,554
Ibyang, Janine, don't fight.

311
00:11:20,638 --> 00:11:21,222
[Oscar] Hey, wait a second.

312
00:11:21,305 --> 00:11:24,308
Your parents might get mad at you.

313
00:11:25,643 --> 00:11:27,144
That's enough.

314
00:11:27,228 --> 00:11:28,187
How about this? Uhm…

315
00:11:29,480 --> 00:11:30,314
Mmm-hmm.

316
00:11:31,107 --> 00:11:32,441
Let's just play hide-and-seek.

317
00:11:33,484 --> 00:11:34,777
And I'll be the seeker.

318
00:11:34,944 --> 00:11:35,611
Okay. Okay.

319
00:11:35,694 --> 00:11:36,612
[Oscar] I'll be the seeker.

320
00:11:36,695 --> 00:11:37,863
- What do you say? Game?
- Okay, game!

321
00:11:37,947 --> 00:11:38,864
Game, game, game, game.

322
00:11:38,948 --> 00:11:39,615
All right, go hide.

323
00:11:40,950 --> 00:11:41,784
Game, huh.

324
00:11:44,370 --> 00:11:47,540
♪ Hide-and-seek under the bright moon ♪

325
00:11:47,623 --> 00:11:50,209
♪ Not behind, not in front ♪

326
00:11:50,793 --> 00:11:51,919
♪ By the time I count to ten ♪

327
00:11:52,002 --> 00:11:53,170
♪ You should already be hiding ♪

328
00:11:53,254 --> 00:11:56,507
♪ One, two, three, four, five ♪

329
00:11:56,590 --> 00:11:59,802
♪ Six, seven, eight, nine, ten! ♪

330
00:12:00,970 --> 00:12:01,929
Go hide now!

331
00:12:02,012 --> 00:12:04,598
[light music playing]

332
00:12:12,148 --> 00:12:13,315
[door closes]

333
00:12:13,399 --> 00:12:14,358
Gavin…

334
00:12:15,693 --> 00:12:17,111
stop packing.

335
00:12:17,194 --> 00:12:18,404
You're not leaving.

336
00:12:19,613 --> 00:12:20,156
Why? I thought…

337
00:12:20,239 --> 00:12:21,031
That’s it.

338
00:12:21,115 --> 00:12:23,451
You're staying in this house,

339
00:12:24,452 --> 00:12:26,704
and you're not telling Atoy

340
00:12:26,787 --> 00:12:29,206
that you were planning to leave.

341
00:12:29,832 --> 00:12:32,501
Wait. I don't understand, Auntie.

342
00:12:32,585 --> 00:12:34,336
What about Miss Cita?

343
00:12:34,420 --> 00:12:36,338
Wouldn't that make her even
angrier with me?

344
00:12:37,047 --> 00:12:38,007
I'll handle that.

345
00:12:38,924 --> 00:12:40,759
You will stay in this room

346
00:12:41,135 --> 00:12:42,803
because I don't want Atoy

347
00:12:42,887 --> 00:12:44,388
giving this room to his guest.

348
00:12:45,389 --> 00:12:45,890
Why, Auntie?

349
00:12:45,973 --> 00:12:47,641
Who's Brother Atoy's guest?

350
00:12:47,725 --> 00:12:50,227
[suspicious music playing]

351
00:12:50,311 --> 00:12:52,146
Atoy! You're here!

352
00:12:52,229 --> 00:12:53,230
Have you been here for a while?

353
00:12:53,314 --> 00:12:53,981
Oh?

354
00:12:54,064 --> 00:12:56,901
Uhm, have you seen Oscar?

355
00:12:56,984 --> 00:12:57,526
[Ame] Who’s Oscar?

356
00:12:57,610 --> 00:13:00,154
Ah, Oka. My friend.

357
00:13:00,237 --> 00:13:01,989
He was here earlier with the kids.

358
00:13:02,072 --> 00:13:05,367
Ahh. Is he the soldier from the news?

359
00:13:05,451 --> 00:13:07,203
The one who was believed dead,

360
00:13:07,286 --> 00:13:08,245
but turned out to be alive?

361
00:13:08,913 --> 00:13:10,372
- He's here now?
- [Atoy]  Mmm-hmm.

362
00:13:12,041 --> 00:13:13,083
Could he have gone outside?

363
00:13:18,297 --> 00:13:18,839
[music fades]

364
00:13:18,923 --> 00:13:21,467
[sneaky music playing]

365
00:13:28,682 --> 00:13:30,851
Got you, Ibyang! Aargh!

366
00:13:32,186 --> 00:13:32,937
Ibyang, sorry.

367
00:13:33,020 --> 00:13:33,979
Oh no. Sorry, sorry.

368
00:13:34,063 --> 00:13:34,897
Are you okay?

369
00:13:35,481 --> 00:13:36,190
Yes, I'm okay.

370
00:13:36,273 --> 00:13:37,107
Sorry, sorry, sorry.

371
00:13:37,191 --> 00:13:40,069
I didn't get hurt.

372
00:13:40,152 --> 00:13:40,903
Okay.

373
00:13:41,487 --> 00:13:42,321
You're amazing.

374
00:13:42,404 --> 00:13:43,614
Your…

375
00:13:43,697 --> 00:13:45,407
your ref…

376
00:13:45,491 --> 00:13:47,993
Lex? Ref-- reflex?

377
00:13:48,077 --> 00:13:50,120
- Oh yes, that's it.
- [chuckles]

378
00:13:50,204 --> 00:13:51,080
You're really good.

379
00:13:51,163 --> 00:13:52,331
Ah, come on. You're even better.

380
00:13:52,915 --> 00:13:53,707
You're so cool.

381
00:13:53,791 --> 00:13:55,376
You're cooler.
You're Atoy's child, after all.

382
00:13:55,459 --> 00:13:56,752
Ibyang!

383
00:13:57,753 --> 00:13:58,295
[music fades]

384
00:13:58,379 --> 00:13:59,630
What are you doing with my child?!

385
00:13:59,713 --> 00:14:01,215
Ibyang, come here!

386
00:14:07,054 --> 00:14:08,180
Audrey, no.

387
00:14:08,889 --> 00:14:10,307
We're just playing.

388
00:14:11,559 --> 00:14:13,602
Stay away from my daughter!

389
00:14:13,686 --> 00:14:15,563
We're just playing.

390
00:14:15,646 --> 00:14:19,066
Stay away from my daughter
and leave my house!

391
00:14:19,149 --> 00:14:20,234
Ouch! Ouch!

392
00:14:20,317 --> 00:14:21,735
Help! Help us!

393
00:14:22,778 --> 00:14:23,320
Help!

394
00:14:23,404 --> 00:14:25,114
Help! I'm going to tell my mom!

395
00:14:28,826 --> 00:14:30,828
Tuy! Tuy!

396
00:14:30,911 --> 00:14:31,745
Yes?

397
00:14:32,997 --> 00:14:33,747
Paldo is right.

398
00:14:33,831 --> 00:14:34,957
You're home.

399
00:14:35,040 --> 00:14:36,750
What happened to you?

400
00:14:36,834 --> 00:14:38,252
Are you okay?

401
00:14:38,711 --> 00:14:40,379
What happened?

402
00:14:40,462 --> 00:14:42,673
You left me all of a sudden.

403
00:14:42,756 --> 00:14:44,967
I thought Samir killed you.

404
00:14:45,050 --> 00:14:46,802
Yes. How did you escape?

405
00:14:46,886 --> 00:14:48,762
Did you hear from Belladonna?

406
00:14:48,846 --> 00:14:50,347
Not yet.

407
00:14:50,431 --> 00:14:51,390
Oh, right.

408
00:14:51,473 --> 00:14:53,350
You saw Okra, right?

409
00:14:53,434 --> 00:14:55,603
Okra? What Okra?

410
00:14:55,686 --> 00:14:56,478
Who's Okra?

411
00:14:56,562 --> 00:14:57,771
What Okra?

412
00:14:57,855 --> 00:15:01,108
Oka is my friend.

413
00:15:06,947 --> 00:15:08,782
Someone's holding a knife!

414
00:15:08,866 --> 00:15:09,408
Someone's stabbing someone!

415
00:15:10,409 --> 00:15:12,786
Hey! What?

416
00:15:12,870 --> 00:15:13,662
You think you're so tough?

417
00:15:15,164 --> 00:15:16,916
Wait, I'll call the police!

418
00:15:16,999 --> 00:15:18,125
What's that?

419
00:15:21,503 --> 00:15:23,464
I'll check.

420
00:15:23,547 --> 00:15:24,381
She's calling me non-stop.

421
00:15:26,926 --> 00:15:30,471
Hello? I told you
to leave it in front of the store.

422
00:15:30,554 --> 00:15:32,681
Yes, I'll get it there.

423
00:15:32,765 --> 00:15:35,309
It's been paid for! I'm repeating my self.

424
00:15:35,935 --> 00:15:37,269
Hey, Gavin!

425
00:15:37,353 --> 00:15:38,812
Gavin! What's that?

426
00:15:38,896 --> 00:15:41,482
That's my friend.

427
00:15:41,565 --> 00:15:43,901
Friend? Is that Okra?

428
00:15:44,610 --> 00:15:46,820
it's Oka not Okra.

429
00:15:51,825 --> 00:15:53,035
Are you okay?

430
00:16:01,210 --> 00:16:03,003
Here, here.

431
00:16:03,087 --> 00:16:04,505
Let me give you medicine.

432
00:16:06,799 --> 00:16:07,591
Does it hurt?

433
00:16:18,560 --> 00:16:20,104
Then I'll lick him.

434
00:16:23,315 --> 00:16:24,441
i'm Emerson.

435
00:16:25,442 --> 00:16:27,069
Just call me Oka.

436
00:16:27,152 --> 00:16:28,904
I feel old when you call me Oka.

437
00:16:29,822 --> 00:16:31,407
Oh, this is…

438
00:16:32,700 --> 00:16:36,078
The one with the picking on
your face is Jesabel.

439
00:16:36,161 --> 00:16:38,414
This is Ame.

440
00:16:39,999 --> 00:16:41,750
The ones who beat you up,

441
00:16:44,086 --> 00:16:45,671
Atoy's cousin, Karla.

442
00:16:45,754 --> 00:16:47,589
And this is Gavin.

443
00:16:47,673 --> 00:16:48,841
Audrey's nephew.

444
00:16:49,466 --> 00:16:51,760
They're dating but they can't.

445
00:16:51,844 --> 00:16:53,137
It's because of Mama.

446
00:16:53,929 --> 00:16:55,597
But I'm really sorry, Oka.

447
00:16:56,390 --> 00:16:59,393
We thought you were one of the goons.

448
00:17:00,352 --> 00:17:04,189
Goons who are handsome and friendly.

449
00:17:04,273 --> 00:17:06,191
And they have a golden heart.

450
00:17:07,026 --> 00:17:08,485
That's crazy.

451
00:17:08,569 --> 00:17:11,655
Ame's just saying whatever
to get back at him.

452
00:17:12,781 --> 00:17:17,036
But to be honest,
you should be afraid of real goons.

453
00:17:17,745 --> 00:17:18,704
What you guys did was cool!

454
00:17:18,787 --> 00:17:21,290
How did you learn to do those moves?

455
00:17:22,791 --> 00:17:24,752
I have personal experience, Oka.

456
00:17:25,335 --> 00:17:27,546
You really know how to beat people up.

457
00:17:28,297 --> 00:17:29,381
No, Oka.

458
00:17:29,465 --> 00:17:31,216
We have a group.

459
00:17:31,300 --> 00:17:32,968
We have missions.

460
00:17:33,052 --> 00:17:35,679
So we can't avoid fighting.

461
00:17:36,680 --> 00:17:38,891
Missions? What's that?

462
00:17:38,974 --> 00:17:39,683
I can join.

463
00:17:39,767 --> 00:17:41,435
What requirements do I need?

464
00:17:42,770 --> 00:17:45,230
You need a codename?

465
00:17:45,981 --> 00:17:48,609
I'm Mini Sinulid.

466
00:17:48,692 --> 00:17:50,861
Emerson is Sinulid 1.

467
00:17:50,944 --> 00:17:52,821
Karla is Sinulid 2.

468
00:17:52,905 --> 00:17:56,200
And Gavin is Adapted Sinulid.

469
00:17:56,283 --> 00:17:57,701
How about you?

470
00:17:57,785 --> 00:17:58,285
I'm fine with being yours.

471
00:17:59,328 --> 00:18:00,662
We want to join!

472
00:18:01,622 --> 00:18:03,207
Yes, let us join the group.

473
00:18:03,832 --> 00:18:04,792
Think of a codename.

474
00:18:04,875 --> 00:18:06,919
I'm… if you're all Sinulids…

475
00:18:09,088 --> 00:18:11,590
Oscarayom. Oscarayom!

476
00:18:11,673 --> 00:18:12,591
That's a good one!

477
00:18:13,926 --> 00:18:16,011
- Oscarayong.
- Right?

478
00:18:16,428 --> 00:18:18,263
They're Sinulids and you're a Karayom…

479
00:18:18,347 --> 00:18:18,931
You get it?

480
00:18:19,014 --> 00:18:21,016
That's a good one!

481
00:18:22,101 --> 00:18:23,393
You're so smart, Corny!

482
00:18:25,562 --> 00:18:27,022
But you're also very witty.

483
00:18:27,106 --> 00:18:29,233
You're so good! I'm proud of you.

484
00:18:29,650 --> 00:18:32,152
You're can't be a part of our group.

485
00:18:33,070 --> 00:18:34,279
You can't be corny.

486
00:18:37,491 --> 00:18:38,450
Wow, you're just so great, huh.

487
00:18:41,328 --> 00:18:43,413
He threatened Ibyang with a knife.

488
00:18:44,081 --> 00:18:45,541
What do you want me to do?

489
00:18:45,624 --> 00:18:48,377
you just saw him holding the knife.

490
00:18:48,460 --> 00:18:50,170
Of course, they're playing.

491
00:18:50,254 --> 00:18:51,213
The knife fell.

492
00:18:51,296 --> 00:18:52,714
And then he caught it.

493
00:18:52,798 --> 00:18:54,341
That doesn't mean he is going to stab her!

494
00:18:54,424 --> 00:18:55,425
Why would he do that?

495
00:18:55,509 --> 00:18:57,511
Why is he playing with our kids?

496
00:18:57,594 --> 00:18:59,638
What's wrong with that?

497
00:18:59,721 --> 00:19:01,765
We're also playing with our children.

498
00:19:01,849 --> 00:19:03,684
My gosh, Atoy.

499
00:19:03,767 --> 00:19:04,977
Don't you find it suspicious

500
00:19:05,060 --> 00:19:09,773
that our daughters
are the ones he's interested in?

501
00:19:09,857 --> 00:19:11,233
- Huh?
- Wait, wait, wait.

502
00:19:11,316 --> 00:19:12,317
What are you saying?

503
00:19:13,068 --> 00:19:15,070
That Oka is a predator?

504
00:19:16,530 --> 00:19:17,906
Audrey, no.

505
00:19:17,990 --> 00:19:18,949
Okay? Impossible.

506
00:19:19,032 --> 00:19:20,159
I know Oka.

507
00:19:20,242 --> 00:19:23,787
She's just a good friend to everyone,
even to the kids.

508
00:19:24,413 --> 00:19:25,539
I don't care.

509
00:19:25,622 --> 00:19:27,416
I don't trust him.

510
00:19:27,499 --> 00:19:29,251
And I don't want him around our daughters.

511
00:19:32,671 --> 00:19:34,506
Audrey, he has no bad intentions

512
00:19:34,590 --> 00:19:35,757
toward our children. Okay?

513
00:19:36,592 --> 00:19:38,468
Look. I understand you. Okay?

514
00:19:38,552 --> 00:19:39,553
I know you still have trauma

515
00:19:39,636 --> 00:19:40,429
because of your brother Red,

516
00:19:40,512 --> 00:19:42,097
because of the business he
got involved in,

517
00:19:42,181 --> 00:19:43,599
and Janine got dragged into it!

518
00:19:43,682 --> 00:19:45,601
But Oka is different.

519
00:19:46,143 --> 00:19:47,978
Okay? He's not doing that.

520
00:19:48,061 --> 00:19:49,605
You know, that's your problem.

521
00:19:50,564 --> 00:19:52,399
You don't listen to me!

522
00:19:53,233 --> 00:19:55,611
I'm your wife, Atoy!

523
00:19:55,694 --> 00:19:57,571
You should take my side!

524
00:19:57,654 --> 00:19:58,155
[scoffs]

525
00:19:58,238 --> 00:19:59,239
Here we go again.

526
00:20:00,741 --> 00:20:03,118
What was that, huh?

527
00:20:03,202 --> 00:20:04,453
What?

528
00:20:05,037 --> 00:20:06,205
I saw that.

529
00:20:06,288 --> 00:20:07,331
[Atoy]  What?

530
00:20:07,414 --> 00:20:09,291
[pensive music playing]

531
00:20:09,374 --> 00:20:10,375
Nothing!

532
00:20:11,793 --> 00:20:12,502
What? Am I wrong again?

533
00:20:12,586 --> 00:20:14,213
It's my fault again?

534
00:20:14,296 --> 00:20:14,880
Well, it's just--

535
00:20:14,963 --> 00:20:16,465
I saw you, Atoy!

536
00:20:16,548 --> 00:20:19,218
Don't shake your head at me like that!

537
00:20:19,301 --> 00:20:20,260
- Okay, fine!
- Say it!

538
00:20:20,344 --> 00:20:21,470
Okay, fine!

539
00:20:21,553 --> 00:20:22,638
Because you're not listening.

540
00:20:23,847 --> 00:20:24,932
You're looking for faults

541
00:20:25,015 --> 00:20:25,807
and you're looking for flaws

542
00:20:25,891 --> 00:20:27,893
in someone who's not doing anything wrong!

543
00:20:28,518 --> 00:20:29,269
You know what, can you not

544
00:20:29,353 --> 00:20:30,854
close off your mind?

545
00:20:30,938 --> 00:20:32,564
Your mind is way too closed, you know.

546
00:20:33,023 --> 00:20:35,067
Audrey, no. Okay?

547
00:20:35,150 --> 00:20:36,777
You got it all wrong.

548
00:20:37,402 --> 00:20:38,987
Oh, have you talked to Ibyang?

549
00:20:39,738 --> 00:20:42,783
Have you asked them what really
happened? Hmm?

550
00:20:43,533 --> 00:20:44,868
Yes.

551
00:20:44,952 --> 00:20:46,203
What did they say?

552
00:20:46,286 --> 00:20:48,956
[suspicious music playing]

553
00:20:49,039 --> 00:20:49,998
Enough.

554
00:20:50,582 --> 00:20:52,167
[Audrey]  It's a mother's instinct.

555
00:20:52,251 --> 00:20:53,835
You have to trust me!

556
00:20:54,378 --> 00:20:56,380
Mother's instinct?

557
00:20:57,089 --> 00:20:58,799
You just misinterpreted it. Okay?

558
00:20:58,882 --> 00:21:01,218
You know what your mother's instinct is?

559
00:21:01,301 --> 00:21:02,469
It's bias!

560
00:21:02,552 --> 00:21:04,221
Because you never really liked Oka, right?

561
00:21:04,304 --> 00:21:05,555
Yes! I don't like him!

562
00:21:06,181 --> 00:21:08,725
Because I don't trust that man!

563
00:21:11,311 --> 00:21:12,020
[music fades]

564
00:21:13,021 --> 00:21:14,815
[heavy music playing]

565
00:21:15,649 --> 00:21:16,483
Oka.

566
00:21:17,067 --> 00:21:19,236
[music continues]

567
00:21:20,153 --> 00:21:20,821
Bro.

568
00:21:21,822 --> 00:21:22,656
Buddy.

569
00:21:23,573 --> 00:21:24,241
Have you been standing there for a while?

570
00:21:24,825 --> 00:21:26,118
Yes, uhm…

571
00:21:26,994 --> 00:21:27,911
I heard everything.

572
00:21:29,121 --> 00:21:30,539
But it's okay.

573
00:21:32,040 --> 00:21:35,127
I understand your wife's concerns.

574
00:21:35,669 --> 00:21:38,130
Audrey, I'm sorry.

575
00:21:39,923 --> 00:21:41,842
It was a mistake for me to come here.

576
00:21:43,844 --> 00:21:45,595
And to you too, Atoy. I'm sorry.

577
00:21:47,514 --> 00:21:49,266
I don't want the two of you

578
00:21:49,349 --> 00:21:50,392
to keep fighting because of me.

579
00:21:51,268 --> 00:21:53,395
So, I'll just leave.

580
00:21:55,647 --> 00:21:57,399
[music continues]

581
00:21:58,734 --> 00:21:59,651
Buddy, wait.

582
00:22:00,986 --> 00:22:03,655
Well, it's a good thing he
volunteered to leave.

583
00:22:04,656 --> 00:22:05,949
[music continues]

584
00:22:17,586 --> 00:22:18,086
[music fades]

585
00:22:18,170 --> 00:22:19,004
[Atoy]  Oka.

586
00:22:20,297 --> 00:22:21,381
Buddy.

587
00:22:21,465 --> 00:22:22,758
[somber music playing]

588
00:22:22,841 --> 00:22:24,134
[Oscar clears throat]

589
00:22:25,218 --> 00:22:26,053
Buddy.

590
00:22:27,512 --> 00:22:29,598
Please forgive Audrey.

591
00:22:30,474 --> 00:22:31,767
Ah, it's okay.

592
00:22:33,143 --> 00:22:34,436
I understand.

593
00:22:36,730 --> 00:22:38,857
what I really regret is…

594
00:22:39,733 --> 00:22:40,901
I thought we'd finally get a chance

595
00:22:40,984 --> 00:22:42,778
to catch up for lost time.

596
00:22:43,111 --> 00:22:44,154
Talk, reminisce.

597
00:22:45,030 --> 00:22:47,574
Have a few drinks, chase girls.

598
00:22:47,657 --> 00:22:49,409
Ah! Just kidding, just kidding.

599
00:22:49,493 --> 00:22:50,827
We're done with that.

600
00:22:50,911 --> 00:22:52,245
[music continues]

601
00:22:52,329 --> 00:22:53,413
So…

602
00:22:54,039 --> 00:22:55,207
Where will you stay now?

603
00:22:57,084 --> 00:22:57,918
I don't know.

604
00:22:58,752 --> 00:23:00,128
Wherever.

605
00:23:04,549 --> 00:23:05,383
No.

606
00:23:06,093 --> 00:23:07,385
Here's what we'll do.

607
00:23:09,096 --> 00:23:11,014
Stay at the shop.

608
00:23:11,098 --> 00:23:12,933
At least you'll have
somewhere to sleep tonight.

609
00:23:13,016 --> 00:23:14,142
You have a shop?

610
00:23:14,935 --> 00:23:15,894
Yeah. It's close by.

611
00:23:17,312 --> 00:23:18,730
[suspicious music playing]

612
00:23:18,814 --> 00:23:20,941
Are you sure Audrey won't get mad at you?

613
00:23:21,858 --> 00:23:24,069
[music continues]

614
00:23:26,822 --> 00:23:27,989
Don't worry about that for now.

615
00:23:29,366 --> 00:23:30,075
I'll take care of her.

616
00:23:30,742 --> 00:23:31,827
Come on.

617
00:23:31,910 --> 00:23:33,829
It'll be good. We can talk there too.

618
00:23:35,163 --> 00:23:36,790
I'll introduce you to the gang.

619
00:23:36,873 --> 00:23:37,999
The people of Tabang Lupa.

620
00:23:42,838 --> 00:23:44,339
Oscar is alive.

621
00:23:45,590 --> 00:23:46,174
Yes.

622
00:23:46,258 --> 00:23:48,802
I know that. I saw that on the news.

623
00:23:49,678 --> 00:23:50,887
Aren't you worried?

624
00:23:51,721 --> 00:23:52,556
No.

625
00:23:54,182 --> 00:23:56,977
Oscar is not important right now.

626
00:23:58,562 --> 00:24:00,981
If he can survive an explosion,

627
00:24:01,064 --> 00:24:02,649
what about Atoy?

628
00:24:03,400 --> 00:24:04,860
[suspicious music playing]

629
00:24:06,069 --> 00:24:07,237
Exactly.

630
00:24:07,320 --> 00:24:09,156
[music continues]

631
00:24:14,953 --> 00:24:19,916
Until I see Atoy's dead body
on the ground…

632
00:24:21,835 --> 00:24:22,752
[music continues]

633
00:24:22,836 --> 00:24:25,505
I will consider him alive.

634
00:24:26,590 --> 00:24:27,674
[swooshes]

635
00:24:27,757 --> 00:24:29,467
[rousing music playing]

636
00:24:29,551 --> 00:24:32,762
[electronic blipping]

637
00:24:40,103 --> 00:24:41,479
[Oscar] You're really lucky, buddy.

638
00:24:41,563 --> 00:24:42,522
You have a family.

639
00:24:42,606 --> 00:24:43,857
You have a business.

640
00:24:43,940 --> 00:24:45,650
One day, you'll find everything

641
00:24:45,734 --> 00:24:46,401
you've been looking for.

642
00:24:46,484 --> 00:24:48,361
[Atoy]  You’ll have all of
that and even more.

643
00:24:48,445 --> 00:24:49,404
You look like someone.

644
00:24:49,487 --> 00:24:50,113
Who?

645
00:24:50,197 --> 00:24:51,907
Our future firstborn child.

646
00:24:51,990 --> 00:24:52,824
[giggles]

647
00:24:52,908 --> 00:24:54,951
Guess who claimed Oscar at the hospital.

648
00:24:55,035 --> 00:24:56,703
[Artem] Anthony Padua.

649
00:24:56,786 --> 00:24:57,746
I know.

650
00:24:57,829 --> 00:24:59,706
I think it is time

651
00:24:59,789 --> 00:25:03,001
to visit our prisoners.

652
00:25:04,127 --> 00:25:06,004
We will make them tell us

653
00:25:06,087 --> 00:25:08,006
who Belladonna is.

654
00:25:08,089 --> 00:25:10,175
Do you know anything about Belladonna?

655
00:25:11,009 --> 00:25:12,594
Have you heard anything about it?

656
00:25:12,677 --> 00:25:13,887
[Audrey]  Atoy is really stubborn.

657
00:25:13,970 --> 00:25:16,097
I already warned him about Oscar.

658
00:25:16,181 --> 00:25:18,225
He seems nice, though. Oscar?

659
00:25:18,308 --> 00:25:21,102
[Cita]  Besides, he wouldn't
be Atoy's friend

660
00:25:21,186 --> 00:25:21,937
if he were a bad person.

661
00:25:22,562 --> 00:25:23,313
Oh!

662
00:25:23,396 --> 00:25:24,147
[thumps]

663
00:25:24,231 --> 00:25:25,815
Oh, 'Toy!

664
00:25:25,899 --> 00:25:26,858
[panicking]

665
00:25:28,693 --> 00:25:30,362
Aargh!

666
00:25:30,445 --> 00:25:33,615
["Mamang Sastre" playing]
